Q:
Find the following limit using either forms or continuity: lim as x -> infinity of (ln(x)+x^2)/((x^7+1)^(1/3)-x)

A:
0

lim as x -> infinity of (ln(x)+x^2)/((x^7+1)^(1/3)-x) ~ lim as x -> infinity of x^2/((x^7+1)^(1/3))

This simplifies further:

lim as x -> infinity of x^2/((x^7)^(1/3)-x) = lim as x -> infinity of x^2/x^(7/3) = lim as x -> infinity of 1/x^(7/3 - 2) = lim as x -> infinity of 1/x^(7/3 - 6/3) = lim as x -> infinity of 1/x^(1/3)

This is form 1/infinity.

Thus lim as x -> infinity of (ln(x)+x^2)/((x^7+1)^(1/3)-x) = 0

